[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there any existing code for (type-indexed) maps between monads? I know category theory has a related definition <code>m ⟶ n</code> (that doesn't enforce monad laws obviously) but this is not even universe-level polymorphic. The main definition I'd like is something along the lines of:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonadHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Bind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun_pure'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">toFun_bind'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;&gt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with maybe a hierarchy along the lines of <code>AddHom</code>/<code>MulHom</code>/etc. for <code>PureHom</code>/<code>MapHom</code>/<code>BindHom</code>/etc.</p>\n<p>If something like this doesn't already exist, I'm also not sure where the appropriate place to open a PR is? It seems like something that could maybe go in batteries or cslib since it doesn't seem especially math focused.</p>",
        "id": 583355153,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1775162585
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonadLift#doc\">docs#MonadLift</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonadLiftT#doc\">docs#MonadLiftT</a> + <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LawfulMonadLift#doc\">docs#LawfulMonadLift</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LawfulMonadLiftT#doc\">docs#LawfulMonadLiftT</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 583362740,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1775165194
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>These all need to be \"canonical\" in the sense of having a correct, inferable instance. I'd like a way to describe more general situations with monad maps that may not be canonical and can vary</p>",
        "id": 583363120,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1775165336
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In particular <code>LawfulMonadLiftT</code> would give rise to a monad map in this style but a given pair of monads with a lift will probably not have a unique mapping between each other</p>",
        "id": 583363568,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1775165504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So for example you might have many maps between <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> which give many induced maps between <code>Option A</code> and <code>ErrorT E B</code></p>",
        "id": 583364722,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1775165894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And I'd like to be able to deduce facts about these maps without making them into full-on monad lifts because they may not be canonical</p>",
        "id": 583364845,
        "sender_full_name": "Devon Tuma",
        "timestamp": 1775165945
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"319772\">Devon Tuma</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Monad-preserving.20morphisms/near/583355153\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[...]<br>\nwith maybe a hierarchy along the lines of <code>AddHom</code>/<code>MulHom</code>/etc. for <code>PureHom</code>/<code>MapHom</code>/<code>BindHom</code>/etc.<br>\n[...]</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Perhaps a <code>Monad.Category</code> per Street:72 <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(72)90019-9\">10.1016/0022-4049(72)90019-9</a>?</p>\n<p>...though the name is probably too ambigious, with the lax/oplax/strict variants</p>\n<p>(EDIT: disregard; missed the universe polymorphism)</p>",
        "id": 583769836,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1775463272
    }
]